.TH BRANDGPT 1 "2024" "BrandGPT CLI" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
brandgpt \- BrandGPT RAG API command-line interface

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B brandgpt
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
[\fIARGS\fR...]

.SH DESCRIPTION
The BrandGPT CLI is a comprehensive command-line interface for interacting with the BrandGPT RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) API. It provides functionality for authentication, document ingestion, session management, and intelligent querying of document collections.

.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.

.TP
.BR \-\-config\-path
Show the path to the configuration file and exit.

.TP
.BR \-\-debug
Enable detailed debug output for troubleshooting.

.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help information and exit.

.SH COMMANDS

.SS Authentication Commands (auth)
Manage user authentication and API keys.

.TP
.B brandgpt auth login
[\fB\-u\fR \fIusername\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR \fIpassword\fR]
[\fB\-s\fR \fIserver\fR]
.br
Login with username and password. Optionally generates an API key for future use.

.TP
.B brandgpt auth register
[\fB\-u\fR \fIusername\fR]
[\fB\-e\fR \fIemail\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR \fIpassword\fR]
[\fB\-s\fR \fIserver\fR]
.br
Register a new user account with input validation.

.TP
.B brandgpt auth set\-key
[\fB\-k\fR \fIapikey\fR]
.br
Set an API key for authentication.

.TP
.B brandgpt auth generate\-key
[\fB\-s\fR \fIserver\fR]
.br
Generate a new API key using existing authentication.

.TP
.B brandgpt auth whoami
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIformat\fR]
[\fB\-s\fR \fIserver\fR]
.br
Display current user information.

.TP
.B brandgpt auth logout
Clear stored authentication credentials.

.SS Session Management Commands (sessions)
Manage document sessions and organization.

.TP
.B brandgpt sessions list
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIformat\fR]
[\fB\-\-limit\fR \fInumber\fR]
.br
List all sessions for the current user.

.TP
.B brandgpt sessions create
[\fB\-n\fR \fIname\fR]
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIformat\fR]
.br
Create a new document session.

.TP
.B brandgpt sessions get
\fIsession\-id\fR
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIformat\fR]
[\fB\-\-include\-docs\fR]
.br
Get detailed information about a specific session.

.TP
.B brandgpt sessions update
\fIsession\-id\fR
[\fB\-n\fR \fIname\fR]
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIformat\fR]
.br
Update session name or properties.

.TP
.B brandgpt sessions delete
\fIsession\-id\fR
[\fB\-f\fR]
.br
Delete a session and all its documents. Use \fB\-f\fR to skip confirmation.

.TP
.B brandgpt sessions docs
\fIsession\-id\fR
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIformat\fR]
.br
List all documents in a specific session.

.SS Data Ingestion Commands (ingest)
Upload and process various types of documents.

.TP
.B brandgpt ingest file
\fIfile\-path\fR
\fB\-s\fR \fIsession\-id\fR
[\fB\-g\fR \fIgroup\-id\fR]
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIformat\fR]
[\fB\-\-wait\fR]
.br
Upload and process a single file.

.TP
.B brandgpt ingest url
\fIurl\fR
\fB\-s\fR \fIsession\-id\fR
[\fB\-g\fR \fIgroup\-id\fR]
[\fB\-d\fR \fIdepth\fR]
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIformat\fR]
[\fB\-\-wait\fR]
.br
Scrape and ingest content from a URL with configurable depth.

.TP
.B brandgpt ingest data
[\fIjson\-file\fR]
\fB\-s\fR \fIsession\-id\fR
[\fB\-g\fR \fIgroup\-id\fR]
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIformat\fR]
[\fB\-\-stdin\fR]
.br
Ingest structured JSON data from file, stdin, or interactive editor.

.TP
.B brandgpt ingest batch
\fIdirectory\fR
\fB\-s\fR \fIsession\-id\fR
[\fB\-g\fR \fIgroup\-id\fR]
[\fB\-\-pattern\fR \fIpattern\fR]
[\fB\-\-recursive\fR]
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIformat\fR]
.br
Upload all matching files from a directory with pattern support.

.TP
.B brandgpt ingest status
\fIsession\-id\fR
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIformat\fR]
.br
Check processing status of documents in a session.

.SS Query and Search Commands (query)
Search and query document collections intelligently.

.TP
.B brandgpt query ask
[\fIquestion\fR]
\fB\-s\fR \fIsession\-id\fR
[\fB\-g\fR \fIgroup\-id\fR]
[\fB\-m\fR \fImax\-results\fR]
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIformat\fR]
[\fB\-\-sources\-only\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-sources\fR]
.br
Ask questions about documents. Interactive mode if no question provided.

.TP
.B brandgpt query search
\fIterms\fR
\fB\-s\fR \fIsession\-id\fR
[\fB\-g\fR \fIgroup\-id\fR]
[\fB\-m\fR \fImax\-results\fR]
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIformat\fR]
[\fB\-\-threshold\fR \fIscore\fR]
.br
Search for specific terms with semantic similarity matching.

.TP
.B brandgpt query chat
\fB\-s\fR \fIsession\-id\fR
[\fB\-g\fR \fIgroup\-id\fR]
[\fB\-m\fR \fImax\-results\fR]
.br
Start an interactive chat session with document context.

.TP
.B brandgpt query batch
\fIquestions\-file\fR
\fB\-s\fR \fIsession\-id\fR
[\fB\-g\fR \fIgroup\-id\fR]
[\fB\-m\fR \fImax\-results\fR]
[\fB\-\-output\fR \fIfile\fR]
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIformat\fR]
[\fB\-\-delay\fR \fIms\fR]
.br
Run multiple queries from a file (one question per line).

.SS Configuration Commands (config)
Manage CLI configuration and settings.

.TP
.B brandgpt config show
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIformat\fR]
.br
Display current configuration with masked sensitive data.

.TP
.B brandgpt config set
\fIkey\fR \fIvalue\fR
.br
Set a configuration value. Valid keys: baseUrl, defaultTimeout, outputFormat.

.TP
.B brandgpt config clear
Clear all configuration settings with confirmation prompt.

.SS Health Check Command
.TP
.B brandgpt health
[\fB\-s\fR \fIserver\fR]
.br
Check API server connectivity and status.

.SH OUTPUT FORMATS
The CLI supports multiple output formats specified with \fB\-\-format\fR:

.TP
.B table
Human-readable tabular format with borders (default)

.TP
.B json
Machine-readable JSON format

.TP
.B yaml
Human-readable YAML format

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.brandgpt/config.json
User configuration file storing API keys, server URLs, and preferences.

.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B DEBUG
Set to any value to enable debug output (equivalent to \fB\-\-debug\fR).

.TP
.B BRANDGPT_BASE_URL
Default server URL for API connections.

.TP
.B BRANDGPT_API_KEY
Default API key for authentication.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Basic authentication and setup:
.nf
brandgpt auth login
brandgpt sessions create \-\-name "My Project"
.fi

.TP
Upload and analyze documents:
.nf
brandgpt ingest file document.pdf \-\-session session\-id
brandgpt query ask "What is the main topic?" \-\-session session\-id
.fi

.TP
Batch processing workflow:
.nf
brandgpt ingest batch ./documents \-\-session session\-id \-\-pattern "*.pdf"
brandgpt ingest status session\-id
echo "What are the key findings?" > questions.txt
brandgpt query batch questions.txt \-\-session session\-id \-\-output results.json
.fi

.TP
Advanced querying with groups:
.nf
brandgpt ingest file legal.pdf \-\-session session\-id \-\-group\-id "legal"
brandgpt ingest file technical.pdf \-\-session session\-id \-\-group\-id "tech"
brandgpt query ask "Legal requirements?" \-\-session session\-id \-\-group\-id "legal"
.fi

.TP
Interactive chat session:
.nf
brandgpt query chat \-\-session session\-id
# Type questions, use 'exit' to quit
.fi

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success

.TP
.B 1
General error (authentication, network, validation, etc.)

.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Use \fB\-\-debug\fR for detailed error information and request/response logging.

Common issues:
.IP \(bu
Authentication errors: Use \fBbrandgpt auth whoami\fR to check status
.IP \(bu
Connection errors: Use \fBbrandgpt health \-\-server URL\fR to test connectivity
.IP \(bu
File upload errors: Check file permissions and path validity
.IP \(bu
Processing delays: Use \fBbrandgpt ingest status session\-id\fR to monitor

